67$ | $3.97$ | $4.24$ |\n| $y$ | $0$ | $-0.48$ | $-0.88$ | $-1.08$ | $-1$ | $-0.55$ | $0.38$ | $1.86$ | $4$ |\n\n$$\n\n$$\n\nPlotting these points, we obtain the following curve:\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14073429/assets/8897c9d1d91007a51d715d982e6b1137bdc5f83f6ef89802b4115522809d4db5.png)" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14073429/state.json" "file_sha256" "8a8bf6720b70a127fff563e34563a58874890bfbd8e1f55c5ec6d04df123712c"} {"question" "q-16192" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14073429/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "c59abd7d6f673481b73098c3b0b57ad19b4515f7214a4c3759965303bb4b5ee6"} {"question" "q-16192" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14073429/state.json" "file_sha256" "8a8bf6720b70a127fff563e34563a58874890bfbd8e1f55c5ec6d04df123712c"} {"question" "q-16192" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["image" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14073429/assets/70df1f5c15d24691c4a8abd56dd78bb36e1c425619751b4afa2e75219d007210.png"] ["image" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14073429/assets/73acda5337e09042efd75d98d7330e85b83024d1660f9286b6812159da9c9879.png"] ["image" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14073429/assets/84c5e6aaa9dfc0312f2a15ed24ce3326f0c811513d3fac22d558bf233fd1b5dc.png"] ["image" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14073429/assets/ac89c944c76160bd9bf67fc48af09d79ddb0092c9a514281c80eec38a3532282.png"] ["image" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14073429/assets/b07c61949971bd6279cd325da58c1db327d95e1f749e09f93748838a18569e72.png"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14073429/state.json" "file_sha256" "8a8bf6720b70a127fff563e34563a58874890bfbd8e1f55c5ec6d04df123712c"} {"question" "q-16192" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/image "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14073429/assets/70df1f5c15d24691c4a8abd56dd78bb36e1c425619751b4afa2e75219d007210.png"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14073429/state.json" "file_sha256" "8a8bf6720b70a127fff563e34563a58874890bfbd8e1f55c5ec6d04df123712c"} {"question" "q-327660" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Given that a curve is defined parametrically as\n\n$$\nx=t-5,\\,y=\\sqrt{\\,t+4\\,}+1,\\,t\\ge -4,\n$$\n\ndetermine the ranges of $x$ and $y.$\n\n$x$\n{{field-1}}{{field-2}}$,\\,y$\n{{field-3}}{{field-4}}" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14073429/state.json" "file_sha256" "8a8bf6720b70a127fff563e34563a58874890bfbd8e1f55c5ec6d04df123712c"} {"question" "q-327660" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Let's consider each variable in turn.\n\n- To find the range of $x,$ note that $t-5\\ge -9$ for all $t\\ge -4.$ Consequently, the range of $x$ is\n\n$$\nx\\ge -9.\n$$\n\n- To find the range of $y,$ note that $\\sqrt{t+4}\\ge 0$ for all $t\\ge -4.$ Consequently, the range of $y$ is\n\n$$\ny\\ge 1.\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14073429/state.json" "file_sha256" "8a8bf6720b70a127fff563e34563a58874890bfbd8e1f55c5ec6d04df123712c"} {"question" "q-327660" "field" nil "attribute" "question/diffi