 <2\\pi ,$ we have $-1\\le \\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta \\le 1.$ Consequently,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-1 & \\le \\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta \\le 1 \\\\ -\\frac{1}{2} & \\le \\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta \\le \\frac{1}{2} \\\\ -\\frac{1}{2} & \\le x\\le \\frac{1}{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, we can conclude that $-\\frac{1}{2}\\le x\\le \\frac{1}{2}.$\n\n- To find the range of $y,$ notice that for $0\\le \\theta <2\\pi ,$ we have $-1\\le \\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta \\le 1.$ Consequently,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-1 & \\le \\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta \\le 1 \\\\ -1+3 & \\le \\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta +3\\le 1+3 \\\\ 2 & \\le y\\le 4.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, we can conclude that $2\\le y\\le 4.$\n\nTherefore, the ranges are $-\\frac{1}{2}\\le x\\le \\frac{1}{2}$ and $2\\le y\\le 4.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14073429/state.json" "file_sha256" "8a8bf6720b70a127fff563e34563a58874890bfbd8e1f55c5ec6d04df123712c"} {"question" "q-123775" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14073429/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "c59abd7d6f673481b73098c3b0b57ad19b4515f7214a4c3759965303bb4b5ee6"} {"question" "q-123775" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14073429/state.json" "file_sha256" "8a8bf6720b70a127fff563e34563a58874890bfbd8e1f55c5ec6d04df123712c"} {"question" "q-123775" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "-2\\le x\\le 2,\\,-3\\le y\\le 3"] ["math" "-2\\le x\\le 2,\\,-4\\le y\\le -2"] ["math" "-\\frac{1}{2}\\le x\\le \\frac{1}{2},\\,-3\\le y\\le 3"] ["math" "-\\frac{1}{2}\\le x\\le \\frac{1}{2},\\,2\\le y\\le 4"] ["math" "1\\le x\\le 3,\\,2\\le y\\le 4"